# Visual acceptance

- Follow `AGENTS.md` and `docs/qa/visual-acceptance.md` for every UI-affecting task.
- Before coding, map each affected surface to agreed design references, concrete
  elements and required states in `docs/qa/visual-review-plan.json`.
- Use ui-craft; colour/token parity alone never proves screen conformity.
- Do not remove or rearrange agreed elements without existing user authorization.
  Document authorized platform/accessibility adaptations individually.
- Post-merge CI must generate fresh APK-free Robolectric PNGs. Never reuse old
  reports, screenshots from another package, or raster mockups as runtime proof.
- Open every required render and its design reference; compare structure, imagery,
  typography, states, clipping and touch targets, including AZ/EN/RU at 100%/150%.
- Missing render/coverage, pending review or unresolved differences block completion.
  Use `review-visual` only after actual inspection; it cannot waive missing evidence.
- Never automatically bless/update baselines to make CI green. Existing gaps in
  `docs/qa/design-discrepancies.md` are debt, not accepted design.
- Report technical CI and visual acceptance separately; cite exact evidence and limits.
